{
  "_comment": [
    "The hand-curated part of the standard British-cryptic abbreviations: the",
    "one- to three-letter chunks a setter may drop into wordplay without",
    "signalling them further. Keys are uppercase letters; values are the",
    "lowercase clue words that stand for them.",
    "",
    "Only what the corpus cannot show lives here: senses fewer than ten clues use",
    "(build_abbreviations.SEEN_MIN), textbook conventions, and spellings",
    "tools/data/lexicons/blocks.json drops the punctuation of. Every reading ten",
    "or more clues use, and every member of build_abbreviations.FAMILIES, joins",
    "it in build_abbreviations.table(), the table every reader uses. Write it",
    "with tools/add_abbreviation.py, which annotators run concurrently.",
    "",
    "tools/clueability.py uses the table as legal charade and container pieces,",
    "and the site's hints and /abbreviations/ page teach it to solvers."
  ],
